---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
const notes = (await getCollection('writing')).length;
const projects = await getCollection('projects');
const nRes = projects.filter((p) => p.data.kind === 'research').length, nProj = projects.filter((p) => p.data.kind === 'project').length;
---
<Base title="About — Hyeonmin Jeon" active="about">
  <div class="wrap about">
    <div class="profile">
      <img class="photo" src="/etc/profile.jpg" alt="Hyeonmin Jeon" width="240" height="240">
      <div>
        <h1>About me</h1>
        <p class="role">Hyeonmin Jeon · 전현민 · M.S. student, Financial Investment AI Lab, Yonsei University</p>
        <div class="bio">
          <p class="thesis">I study decision-making under uncertainty when the uncertainty itself must first be learned from data.</p>
          <p class="kw">Generative models as simulation inputs · Ranking &amp; selection · Input uncertainty · Simulation optimisation</p>
          <p>I studied electrical engineering mainly because it was my major. That changed at GAIL, an AI lab at Chung-Ang University, where I started leading small projects of my own and found that I liked building a model and checking it against what actually happens. In my master's I moved into finance and built generative models for portfolio risk. What stayed with me was taking a method into a domain it was not built for. Now I want to carry that back to engineering systems.</p>
          <p>In the lab I also work on applied projects: a TIPS-funded engine with an industry partner that describes, classifies and generates an artist's style with Qwen vision-language models and diffusion, and a stock-recommendation system in which I extend the open-source TradingAgents framework from a single recommendation into a simulated market of LLM agents. What I take from both is the same habit: a model is only as useful as the check it survives.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="hsec"><h2>What I work on</h2>
      <ul class="how">
        <li><b>Generative models behind a decision.</b> <a href="/research/diffusion-scenarios/">CASE</a> generates multi-asset return scenarios and is judged by the risk reserve set on them; <a href="/research/tailflow/">TailFlow</a> asks the same question in a market whose true VaR/ES is known.</li>
        <li><b>How far learned uncertainty travels.</b> A <a href="/research/model-uncertainty-priors/">learned prior</a> for Bayesian factor selection, and how much of a selection guarantee survives a fitted input model (<a href="/research/input-uncertainty-select/">Input-Uncertainty Select</a>, <a href="/research/rs-lab/">rs-lab</a>).</li>
        <li><b>The same method in new domains.</b> A <a href="/projects/nune-retina-rl/">hospital exam-room scheduler</a>, <a href="/projects/eco-route-rl/">low-CO₂ routing</a>, and three battery projects ending in <a href="/research/battery-os-efficiency/">Battery and the OS</a>.</li>
        <li><b>Agents that read the market live.</b> <a href="/projects/fomc-live-desk/">FOMC Live Desk</a> turns a live broadcast into a transcript, scores each sentence with a fast decision model and lets TradingAgents-based market participants react.</li>
        <li><b>Tools I use myself.</b> <a href="/projects/lucubra/">Lucubra</a>, a research-agent platform that checks a draft's numbers the way a referee would.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="hsec"><h2>How I work</h2>
      <ul class="how">
        <li><b>Every number has a file.</b> Each figure and metric on this site comes from a script and a result file in the repository.</li>
        <li><b>Negative results stay.</b> When a method does not do what was hoped, the write-up says so, with the numbers.</li>
        <li><b>Truth first, then the real thing.</b> Methods are tested where the answer is known before they meet the real problem.</li>
        <li><b>Data comes in the front door.</b> No data obtained by working around an access control; {notes} reading notes are on the <a href="/blog/">blog</a>.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="hsec"><h2>Now</h2>
      <ul class="how">
        <li><b>Papers.</b> One under review at ESWA, one submitted to Applied Soft Computing, two working papers (<a href="/publications/">status</a>).</li>
        <li><b>Batteries.</b> Personal projects back toward electrical engineering, most recently <a href="/research/battery-os-efficiency/">what the M1's SoC and OS do for battery ageing</a>.</li>
        <li><b>Lab projects.</b> The <a href="/projects/artist-style-engine/">artist-style engine</a> (TIPS, with Urban Complex) and a TradingAgents-based market simulation for stock recommendation.</li>
        <li><b>Lab.</b> Research assistant since March 2025; TA for undergraduate Financial Engineering, spring 2026.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="hsec"><h2>Path so far</h2>
      <ul class="cv">
        <li><span class="d">2025.03 –</span><div>M.S., Industrial Engineering — Financial Investment AI Lab, Yonsei University<div class="k">Diffusion transformers for scenario generation, phase-preserving timing measurement, learned priors for factor selection; talk at ISF 2025, Beijing, with SAS Institute</div></div></li>
        <li><span class="d">2022.12 – 2024.12</span><div>Undergraduate researcher, GAIL, Chung-Ang University<div class="k">Computer vision and generative models — diffusion oversampling (KICS 2023), a lifelog sleep-score model (ETRI challenge), a latent-diffusion portfolio study, 3D point clouds</div></div></li>
        <li><span class="d">2023.04 – 12</span><div>Team lead, Green-Navi — Carbon-Neutral ESG Practical-Problem Research Group, Chung-Ang University<div class="k">Reinforcement learning for fuel-optimal urban routing; presented at the research fair 2023.11.02 — later rebuilt as <a href="/projects/eco-route-rl/">Eco-Route RL</a></div></div></li>
        <li><span class="d">2020.03 – 2021.09</span><div>Mandatory military service, Republic of Korea</div></li>
        <li><span class="d">– 2025.02</span><div>B.S., School of Electrical and Electronics Engineering, Chung-Ang University</div></li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="hsec"><h2>Looking ahead</h2>
      <div class="prose-lite"><p>I want to keep the method and change the domain: learn the theory and data a new field asks for, and find out which parts of this way of working survive the move.</p></div>
    </div>

    <div class="hsec"><h2>See the work</h2>
      <ul class="feat feat2">
        <li><a class="card" href="/research/"><img src="/projects/diffusion-scenarios/media/architecture.png" alt="CASE architecture" loading="lazy"></a>
          <div class="kick"><span>Research</span><span>{nRes} write-ups</span></div>
          <a class="t" href="/research/">Research →</a>
          <p class="k">Papers and research threads: generative scenarios, learned priors, selection with guarantees, batteries.</p></li>
        <li><a class="card" href="/projects/"><img src="/projects/lucubra/media/home.jpg" alt="Lucubra home screen" loading="lazy"></a>
          <div class="kick"><span>Projects</span><span>{nProj} projects</span></div>
          <a class="t" href="/projects/">Projects →</a>
          <p class="k">Things I built: a research-agent platform, a hospital scheduler, routing in a traffic simulator, the lab's projects.</p></li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="hsec"><h2>Contact</h2>
      <p class="contact-line"><a href="mailto:hyeonmin16@yonsei.ac.kr">hyeonmin16@yonsei.ac.kr</a> · <a href="/cv/">CV</a> · <a href="/research/">Research</a> · <a href="/projects/">Projects</a></p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
